.TH MATH.H 3v32 "October 11, 2026" "Vircon32 DevTools 26.04.24" "Vircon32 C Library"
.SH NAME
math.h \- Vircon32 arithmetic, rounding, trigonometric and exponential functions
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include \(dqmath.h\(dq
.PP
.B "#define pi       3.1415926"
.B "#define INT_MIN  0x80000000"
.B "#define INT_MAX  2147483647"
.PP
.BI "int   min( int " a ", int " b " );"
.BI "int   max( int " a ", int " b " );"
.BI "int   abs( int " a " );"
.BI "float fmin( float " x ", float " y " );"
.BI "float fmax( float " x ", float " y " );"
.BI "float fabs( float " x " );"
.BI "float fmod( float " x ", float " y " );"
.PP
.BI "float floor( float " x " );"
.BI "float ceil( float " x " );"
.BI "float round( float " x " );"
.PP
.BI "float sin( float " angle " );"
.BI "float cos( float " angle " );"
.BI "float tan( float " angle " );"
.BI "float asin( float " x " );"
.BI "float acos( float " x " );"
.BI "float atan2( float " y ", float " x " );"
.PP
.BI "float sqrt( float " x " );"
.BI "float pow( float " x ", float " y " );"
.BI "float exp( float " x " );"
.BI "float log( float " x " );"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Each function is one or a few of the CPU's own instructions, so they
are cheap, but they are single-precision (32-bit
.BR float )
and some stop the program with a hardware error where the standard C
functions would return NaN or infinity (see
.BR "HARDWARE ERRORS" ).
Angles are in radians.
.TP
.BR min ", " max ", " fmin ", " fmax
The smaller or larger of two values, for
.B int
and
.B float
respectively. (Standard C has
.B fmin
and
.B fmax
but no
.B min
or
.BR max .)
.TP
.BR abs ", " fabs
Absolute value.
.TP
.B fmod
The remainder of
.IR x / y ,
with the sign of
.IR x .
.TP
.BR floor ", " ceil ", " round
Round down, up, or to the nearest whole number, returning a
.BR float .
Convert to
.B int
with a cast or an assignment, which truncates toward zero.
.TP
.BR sin ", " cos ", " tan
Sine, cosine and tangent.
.B cos
is computed as
.IR sin(angle + pi/2) ,
and
.B tan
as their quotient.
.TP
.BR asin ", " acos
Arc sine and arc cosine, for
.I x
from \-1 to 1.
.TP
.B atan2
The angle of the vector
.RI ( x ", " y ),
from \-pi to pi.
.TP
.B sqrt
Square root, computed as
.IR pow(x,\ 0.5) .
.TP
.BR pow ", " exp
.I x
raised to
.IR y ,
and
.I e
raised to
.IR x .
.TP
.B log
Natural logarithm.
.SH HARDWARE ERRORS
These calls stop the program with a hardware error (see
.BR vircon32 (3v32)):
.BR fmod "(x, 0),"
.B tan
where the computed cosine is exactly 0,
.BR asin " and " acos
of values outside \-1 to 1,
.BR atan2 "(0, 0),"
.B sqrt
of a negative number,
.B pow
of a negative number to a non-integer power,
.B log
of 0 or a negative number.
.SH NOTES
.B INT_MIN
is written in hexadecimal because the compiler would read
.I \-2147483648
as the negation of a number too large for an
.BR int .
.PP
Division by zero with the
.B /
operator (on integers or floats) or the
.B %
operator (integers only; use
.B fmod
for floats) also stops the program.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vircon32 (3v32),
.BR math.hpp (3v32)
.SH AUTHOR
The Vircon32 standard library was written by Javier Carracedo
.RI ( Carra ).
This manual page was written by Matthew Haas for the v32c++ project.
